<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ram Khamhaeng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1237–<a href="/years/1298">1298</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Ram Khamhaeng the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ram Khamhaeng was the third king of Sukhothai, reigning from about 1279 to 1298, under whom the Thai kingdom expanded widely. Tradition credits him with creating the Thai script, recorded in the Ram Khamhaeng inscription. He was an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mangrai">Mangrai</a> of Lan Na and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngam-mueang">Ngam Mueang</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phayao">Phayao</a> and is said to have helped found Chiang Mai in 1296.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ram-khamhaeng.jpg" alt="Ram Khamhaeng" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This Photo was taken by Supanut Arunoprayote. … · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram_Khamhaeng_the_Great_(I).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Tradition holds that he chose the site in consultation with his allies Ngam Mueang of Phayao and <b>Ram Khamhaeng of Sukhothai</b>, with whom he had sworn friendship.</blockquote><a href="/empire/lan-na">Lan Na · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Ram Khamhaeng</b>'s inscription says a bell hung at the palace gate so that any subject with a grievance could ring it and be heard by the king.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sukhothai-kingdom">Sukhothai Kingdom · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Its best-known ruler, Ngam Mueang, was an ally of Mangrai of Lan Na and <b>Ram Khamhaeng of Sukhothai</b>; the three are said to have sworn friendship around 1287, an event commemorated by the Three Kings Monument in Chiang Mai.</blockquote><a href="/state/phayao-kingdom">Phayao Kingdom</a></li></ul></section>
